  "id": "COMPOUND:3263 - PROTEIN:601",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADPH) interacts with NADH dehydrogenase [ubiquinone] iron-sulfur protein 7, mitochondrial. This interaction is mediated through a series of targets, with NADPH acting as a substrate for 8-oxo-dGTP diphosphatase, which in turn is targeted by 2,4-Diamino-6-[N-(3',5'-Dimethoxybenzyl)-N-Methylamino]Pyrido[2,3-D]Pyrimidine and 6-(Octahydro-1h-Indol-1-Ylmethyl)Decahydroquinazoline-2,4-Diamine. These compounds appear to inhibit the enzyme NADH dehydrogenase [ubiquinone] iron-sulfur protein 7, mitochondrial, suggesting a pathway where NADPH may influence the activity of this mitochondrial enzyme. The evidence is consistent with a role in metabolic regulation, as NADH dehydrogenase is involved in the electron transport chain and energy production. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of structurally diverse compounds further support a mechanism that is both specific and biologically relevant. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for NADPH in modulating mitochondrial function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
